=== PART 1: the χ=3 floor IS the cyclotomic locus  (z^7 − z) ===
  hexagon+center: 7 points (6 sixth-roots of unity + origin), 12 unit edges
  degree sequence = [6, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3]  (hub deg 6 + 6-cycle deg 3 = wheel W6)
  χ(hexagon+center) = 3   [W6: even 6-cycle needs 2, hub forces a 3rd]
  these 7 points = roots of z^7 − z = z·(z^6 − 1):  max|r^7 − r| = 3.08e-15
  over F_7:  z^7 − z ≡ ∏_(a∈F_7)(z−a)  (z^7≡z ∀a∈F_7): True  ⟹ roots = the 7 colors
  so z^7−z gives the χ=3 gadget over ℂ AND the 7-coloring palette over F_7.
  7 = 6+1 (FTA: hexagon z^6−1 times the center z) = Φ_3(2) = |PG(2,2)| (HYP-1043/1104).

=== PART 2: χ=4 (Moser spindle) requires a NON-cyclotomic rotation ===
  Moser spindle: 7 vertices, 11 unit edges; far-vertex gap |(1+ζ6) − e^(iθ)(1+ζ6)| = 1.000000
  χ(Moser spindle) = 4   (minimal χ=4 unit-distance graph)
  spindle angle θ = 0.585686 rad = 33.557°,  cos θ = 0.833333 (= 5/6)
  cos θ = 5/6 ∉ {0,±1/2,±1}  ⟹  by Niven θ is an IRRATIONAL multiple of π (θ/π ∉ ℚ).
  e^(iθ) = (5 + i√11)/6 = 0.833333+0.552771j;  check |e^(iθ)−rot| = 1.57e-16
  3·(e^(iθ))² − 5·e^(iθ) + 3 = 0.00e+00  ⟹ e^(iθ) is a root of 3z²−5z+3
  3z²−5z+3: discriminant = -11 = −11; Mahler measure = leading_coeff·∏max(1,|root|) = 3·1·1 = 3 > 1
  ⟹ by Kronecker, e^(iθ) is NOT a root of unity (non-cyclotomic unit-circle point).
  rhombi ∈ ℚ(√−3) (Eisenstein), rotation ∈ ℚ(√−11) ⟹ spindle lives in ℚ(√−3, √−11);
  both −3, −11 are HEEGNER numbers. χ≥4 needs the 2nd field — ℤ[ζ6] alone is 3-colorable.
  rhombus A ⊂ ℤ[ζ6]? True;  rotated far vertex B[3] ∈ ℤ[ζ6]? False  (False = it left the lattice)

=== PART 3: FTA/spectral bridge — roots of unity ARE the eigenvalues ===
  C6(1) (hexagon, no center) eigenvalues = connection poly (z + 1/z) at 6th roots of unity
     = {2cos(πj/3)} = [-2.0, -1.0, 1.0, 2.0];  λ_max=2.0, λ_min=-2.0
  Hoffman: χ ≥ 1 − λ_max/λ_min = 1 − 2.0/-2.0 = 2 (tight: bipartite 6-cycle)
  m→∞ (6m-th roots → the full unit circle): connection poly → Bessel J0 = the plane's
  symbol (λ_min≈−0.4028 ⟹ χ(ℝ²)≥3.48, S699g/HYP-2264). The FTA root locus IS the spectrum.
